  "instance_name": "emotional_instability_stereotype",
  "label": "Emotional Instability Stereotype",
  "description": "This stereotype involves labeling individuals as 'crazy,' 'hysterical,' or 'volatile' to imply they are emotionally unstable or unpredictable. It is often used to demean or dehumanize people, particularly in contexts where their behavior is perceived as erratic or out of control. This stereotype is part of broader misogynistic tropes that associate women (and sometimes men) with emotional instability, which can lead to social harm or reinforce negative societal perceptions.",
